// Native CLI-contract fixture (Severed Chains Native, no upstream origin).
// NOT oracle-derived: this pins the native exit-status contract, not reference output.
//
// `include missing_lib.fate;` names a file that exists nowhere, so a run with a usable
// include path still compiles and answers with `Failed to load include` plus
// `unknown function helper` (exit 3). With a `-L` path that is not a directory it must
// stop before the program text is discussed: exit 2, nothing written. The fixture has to
// be compilable for that reason - otherwise it would pin a path the check cannot reach.
include missing_lib.fate;
def f(a) {
  helper(a);
  return;
}
